    id: 'aig-goldman-cds-2008', title: 'AIG Financial Products: CDS Termination Through Maiden Lane III',
    era: '2008–2014', year: 2008, country: 'United States', flag: '🇺🇸', category: 'CDS Exposure & Asset-Financed Resolution',
    evidence: 'New York Fed Maiden Lane transaction overview, facility terms and repayment milestones.',
    crisis_window: 'During the 2008 crisis, CDS contracts written by AIG Financial Products created capital and liquidity pressure on AIG. Maiden Lane III purchased underlying CDOs to enable termination of associated CDS contracts.',
    insiders: ['AIG (parent firm facing capital and liquidity pressure; $5 billion equity contributor)', 'AIG Financial Products (writer of CDS contracts terminated through the transaction)', 'AIGFP counterparties (sellers of multi-sector CDOs to Maiden Lane III)', 'Maiden Lane III LLC (asset-purchasing vehicle)', 'Federal Reserve Bank of New York (senior lender and oversight institution)', 'Federal Reserve Board (authority authorizing the crisis lending vehicles)', 'US public (recipient of reported New York Fed net gains and bearer of public lending exposure)'],
    quid_pro_quo: 'Maiden Lane III purchased $29.3 billion in multi-sector CDOs from certain AIGFP counterparties. The New York Fed lent approximately $24.3 billion and AIG supplied $5 billion in equity, allowing associated CDS contracts to terminate.',
    theft_mechanism: 'Public senior lending and private equity financed asset purchases intended to relieve derivatives-related liquidity pressure. This establishes a risk-transfer and resolution mechanism, not by itself a finding of theft or misconduct by a named counterparty.',
    who_gained: 'AIG obtained relief from the relevant CDS obligations and counterparties sold assets. The New York Fed reports full repayment with interest and approximately $6.6 billion in net gains for the US public after asset sales; these are vehicle-specific outcomes.',
    who_lost: 'The public lender bore risk while loans were outstanding. Gross assistance is not a realized taxpayer loss: the source reports repayment. It does not quantify losses elsewhere in AIG, counterparty net profits or homeowner losses attributable to this transaction.',
    legacy: 'Illustrates an asset-backed crisis vehicle with senior-lender priority and a separate equity contribution. Lending exposure, purchase prices, collateral already posted and final recoveries must not be conflated.',
    caveat: 'Reviewed the transaction overview, not counterparty payment schedules, valuation files or SIGTARP findings. It does not identify Goldman Sachs in the reviewed overview or establish par-value terms, negotiation conduct, executive compensation or current litigation status. This source alone cannot answer distributional criticisms of the broader AIG rescue.',
    sources: [{ publisher: 'Federal Reserve Bank of New York', title: 'Maiden Lane Transactions — facility overview and repayment milestones', url: 'https://www.newyorkfed.org/markets/maidenlane' }]
