    crisis_window: 'Khedive Isma\'il defaulted on Egypt\'s foreign debts — owed mostly to British and French creditors — after a modernization drive (railways, telegraphs, irrigation, the Suez Canal) had been financed by European loans. On 2 May 1876 he issued a decree establishing the Caisse de la Dette Publique, an international commission to supervise Egypt\'s debt payments and investigate what Egypt could afford, how taxes were collected, the size of the floating debt, and how the debt had been incurred.',
